  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district (treated as cash). Governmental lines from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (p5), Total Governmental Funds column, which is after the Eliminations column (2,000,000 Building and grounds and 250,000 Extracurricular transfers eliminated; transfers in total column are zero, so transfers_in/out are null). Beginning/ending cash = fund balances 16,157,435 / 23,985,667 (all cash; balance sheet p4 shows cash plus cash with county treasurers). Business-type = Nutrition Fund (p6-7); measure recorded as cash (no liabilities, net position equals cash). Nutrition Fund total operating receipts 2,642,171 less disbursements 2,918,458 reconciles 1,139,136 to 862,849. Balance sheet uses Statement of Net Position primary government Total column (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) is more detailed than fund statement; its Building and grounds 4,812,068 includes the 2,000,000 transfer to Depreciation Fund (p5 elimination), split into expenditure 2,812,068 and other financing -2,000,000; Transfers 250,000 recorded as other financing -250,000; the printed total 46,738,812 includes both transfers. Depreciation Fund and Other Governmental Funds combining (4 funds) also recorded. Other-fund Federal programs/State categorical function guesses flagged. Read pages 1-10 of 10.",
